Adaptive Cards do not have a direct property to change the background color of the entire card. However, you can achieve a similar effect using several techniques:

**1. Using a FactSet with a Background Color:**

This is the most common and recommended approach.  You wrap the entire content of your Adaptive Card within a `FactSet` element and apply a background color to it.

```json
{
  "type": "AdaptiveCard",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "FactSet",
      "facts": [
        {
          "title": "My Card",
          "value": "This is the content of my card."
        }
      ],
      "style": "attention"  // or "good", "warning", "accent"
    },
    {
      "type": "TextBlock",
      "text": "More content here..."
    }
  ],
  "backgroundImage": "https://example.com/image.jpg" // Optional background image
}
```

* **`style` property:**  The `style` property of the `FactSet` controls the background color.  Available styles are:
    * `"attention"`: Red background
    * `"good"`: Green background
    * `"warning"`: Yellow background
    * `"accent"`: Blue background
* **Limitations:** This approach only provides a limited set of predefined background colors.  You can't specify a custom hex code or RGB value directly.
* **`backgroundImage`:**  You can also use a background image in addition to the `FactSet` style.  The `FactSet` style will be applied on top of the image.

**2. Using a Container with a Background Color (Microsoft Teams and some other renderers):**

Some renderers (like Microsoft Teams) support a `Container` element with a `background` property. This is the closest you'll get to a direct background color setting.

```json
{
  "type": "AdaptiveCard",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "Container",
      "background": "FFFFFF", // Hex code for white
      "padding": "10px",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "TextBlock",
          "text": "This is the content of my card."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

* **`background` property:**  Accepts a hex code (e.g., "FFFFFF" for white, "000000" for black

